## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop**: `newGame()` builds single `S` object; `rand(S)` mulberry32-style PRNG seeded from `S.rngState`; `beginTurn()/finishTurn()` calls storm→event→production→needs→fatigueSkill→migration→tradeTick→tickTimers in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 — Map**: `NT=64` (8x8), `genMap()` uses `rand(S)` for terrain; `tryBuild()` checks `B.terr.includes(t.terr)`; `adjInfo()` multiplier fed into production `mult` calc. Score 2.

**F3 — Economy**: forge `ore+power→metal`, workshop `metal+power→parts`, greenhouse `soil+water→food`, sifter `ash→soil`; `applyCaps()` clamps and logs overflow. Score 2.

**F4 — Population**: colonist records `{skill,fatigue,morale,job,at}`; `skillMult()`/`fatigueMult()` read `c.skill`/`c.fatigue` inside `production()`. Score 2.

**F5 — Needs**: `needs()` consumes 1 food/water per colonist per turn; shortage does `c.morale-=12/-8`; `moraleMult(c)` used in production; fed&watered grants `+3` morale (gradual recovery). Score 2.

**F6 — Research**: `RESEARCH` has 10 nodes; `tryResearch()` enforces `R.req`; cost deducted; `researchMult()` reads `hasR()` flags and multiplies output in `production()`. Score 2.

**F7 — Events**: 12 entries in `EVENTS`; weighted pick in `drawEvent()` via `e.w`; 5 events (`wanderers,cache,fever,preacher,deserter`) have 2-3 choices mutating state differently; `S.eventCds[ev.id]=EVENT_CD` cooldown. Score 2.

**F8 — Trade**: `priceOf()` reads `S.res[g]/capFor()` scarcity and `T.drift[g]`; `T.stock[g]` decremented on buy, capped by `CARAVAN_STOCK`; `doBuy()`/`doSell()` both wired to UI buttons. Score 2.

**F9 — Hazard**: `stormResolve()` fires on `S.stormNext`; `stormSeverity(turn)` grows with turn/12; knocked-out (`t.dis`) buildings produce zero in `production()`; `forecast`/`reinforce` research and Storm Wall reduce damage; `tryRepair()` spends parts + idle labor and clears `dis`. Score 2.

**F10 — Save/load**: `serialize(S)`→textarea; `tryLoad()` parses JSON, `validateState()` checks schema, `$('savemsg')` shows `'✗ '+r.err` on bad input. Score 2.

**F11 — End conditions**: lose at `S.colonists.length===0`→`S.dead=true`; win at turn 60 via `S.winFlag=...`; `calcScore()` combines pop/research/stock/turns/win; `showSummary()` renders result. Score 2.

**F12 — UI**: `data-act="tab:..."` switching; `renderLog()` prefixes `'T'+l.t`; `data-tip` tooltips throughout header/tiles/research; keydown handles Space and `1`-`6`; narrow-screen media query adjusts table/chip sizing. Score 2.

**F13 — Dev panel**: `runTests()` asserts real invariants (no negative resources, cap respect, roster consistency, cooldowns, save/load hash match); `runBenchmark()`/`benchRun()` runs headless 200-turn loop and prints `stateHash()`. Score 2.

**G1**: `researchMult(S,key)` reads `hasR(S,'ashfilter')` etc., multiplied into `mult` in `production()` every relevant building each turn. Score 4.

**G2**: `needs()` shortage → `c.morale-=12/-8`; `moraleMult(c)` factors into `production()` mult; `morale<=0` fully blocks output (`refuses to work`). Score 4.

**G3**: `stormResolve()` reduces `t.hp`, sets `t.dis` at 0hp; `production()` skips output only when `t.dis` (binary, not proportional to partial damage); `tryRepair()` costs parts+fatigue and restores. Minor gap: partial damage doesn't reduce output. Score 3.

**G4**: `priceOf()` = `TRADE_BASE[g]*T.drift[g]*scarcity(S.res[g]/cap)`; `T.drift` updates each caravan cycle via `rand()`; feeds `buyPrice/sellPrice` used in `doBuy/doSell`. Score 4.

**G5**: `wanderers` choice pushes new colonists / `addRes(food)` / `allMorale`; `cache` choice mutates `S.res.metal/parts` and colonist fatigue — real state writes, not just log. Score 4.

